VALUES (460091210101015, ARRAY['"A citizen damages public property during a protest. Which Fundamental Duty is most directly relevant to the conduct?"'::jsonb, '"A state policy seeks environmental improvement, but an official arbitrarily denies access to a public benefit. What is a balanced analysis?"'::jsonb, '"A constitutional amendment changes the composition of a body, and challengers claim the change damages separation of powers and judicial review. What evidence is most important to the basic-structure question?"'::jsonb, '"Who chaired the Drafting Committee of the Constituent Assembly?"'::jsonb, '"A Fundamental Right is asserted against a policy goal in Part IV. Which reading method best reflects the constitutional relationship?"'::jsonb, '"A citizen''s speech is restricted by a law. Which is the most accurate way to evaluate the restriction under Article 19?"'::jsonb, '"India is described in the Preamble as a:"'::jsonb, '"A student says that because the Constitution is written, every rule must appear in one unamended original document. Which correction is best?"'::jsonb, '"A citizen challenges an order affecting personal liberty. The authority claims Article 21 only applies when a law is completely absent, not when procedure exists but is arbitrary. Which response best reflects modern constitutional reasoning at course level?"'::jsonb, '"Who is the constitutional head of a state in India?"'::jsonb, '"A claimant argues that because a policy appears in Part IV, courts must enforce it as if it were a Fundamental Right. Which constitutional text most directly challenges that claim?"'::jsonb, '"A government scheme promotes social welfare, but its implementation treats similarly situated citizens arbitrarily. Which constitutional analysis is strongest?"'::jsonb, '"Which part opens the Constitution of India and states its guiding ideals?"'::jsonb, '"An amendment changes an institution in a way alleged to eliminate judicial review and constitutional limits. Which framework most directly addresses whether a constitutional amendment can destroy foundational features?"'::jsonb, '"A public authority refuses the same legal protection to two people in materially identical circumstances without a relevant reason. Which constitutional principle is most directly raised?"'::jsonb, '"A student argues that the Preamble itself grants an unlimited legal power to an executive agency. What is the key flaw?"'::jsonb, '"An official says Article 14 guarantees identical treatment even where relevant circumstances differ. Which statement is more accurate?"'::jsonb, '"A teacher is describing an amendment''s constitutional history. Which pair is correct?"'::jsonb, '"Which Article protects specified freedoms, subject to constitutional restrictions?"'::jsonb, '"A person says all Directive Principles are individually enforceable in court because they are ''fundamental in governance''. Which reasoning corrects the conflation?"'::jsonb, '"A school textbook says Fundamental Duties were added to the Constitution through an amendment. Which pairing is correct?"'::jsonb, '"Which Article guarantees equality before the law and equal protection of the laws?"'::jsonb, '"When did the Constitution of India come into force?"'::jsonb, '"The Constitution''s Preamble is invoked to interpret an ambiguous provision. Which description best fits its role?"'::jsonb, '"A new state policy is consistent with a Directive Principle but is implemented in a way that violates Article 21. What follows?"'::jsonb, '"What is the principal purpose of a constitution?"'::jsonb, '"A Fundamental Duty to protect the environment is cited to automatically deny a person''s otherwise lawful speech. Which conclusion is most careful?"'::jsonb, '"Which Article protects life and personal liberty?"'::jsonb, '"Fundamental Rights are primarily contained in which Part of the Constitution?"'::jsonb, '"A law restricts a citizen''s speech to address a public concern. The citizen argues Article 19 makes all restrictions invalid. Which reasoning is most defensible?"'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Duty to vote in every election as stated in Article 51A"'::jsonb, '"Duty to serve as a judge"'::jsonb, '"Duty to safeguard public property and abjure violence"'::jsonb, '"Duty to protect the environment only"'::jsonb, '"Assume Fundamental Duties erase all legal procedures"'::jsonb, '"Assume Article 14 applies only during elections"'::jsonb, '"Treat the environmental aim as an automatic exemption from equality"'::jsonb, '"Recognize the environmental aim and Article 51A duty, while also assessing whether the decision complies with applicable rights such as Article 14"'::jsonb, '"The amendment''s actual legal effects on the alleged foundational features, considered under the basic-structure doctrine"'::jsonb, '"How many local wards exist"'::jsonb, '"Whether the amendment uses formal language"'::jsonb, '"Whether a state Governor publicly supports the amendment"'::jsonb, '"Jawaharlal Nehru"'::jsonb, '"B. R. Ambedkar"'::jsonb, '"Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel"'::jsonb, '"Rajendra Prasad"'::jsonb, '"Read the provisions harmoniously, recognizing enforceable rights and the directive role of Part IV"'::jsonb, '"Always disregard Part IV"'::jsonb, '"Assume both Parts have identical justiciability"'::jsonb, '"Treat Directive Principles as criminal offences"'::jsonb, '"Article 19 permits no restrictions in any circumstances"'::jsonb, '"Check the relevant freedom and whether the restriction fits a constitutionally permitted ground and is reasonable"'::jsonb, '"Treat Article 19 as a duty rather than a right"'::jsonb, '"Any restriction is automatically unconstitutional"'::jsonb, '"Presidential Kingdom"'::jsonb, '"Sovereign Socialist Secular Democratic Republic"'::jsonb, '"Confederation of Provinces"'::jsonb, '"Federal Monarchy"'::jsonb, '"Written constitutions can be amended according to their prescribed procedures"'::jsonb, '"Written constitutions cannot change"'::jsonb, '"Only Governors can amend the Constitution"'::jsonb, '"Amendments automatically replace all Fundamental Rights"'::jsonb, '"Any written procedure automatically validates every deprivation"'::jsonb, '"Article 21 only applies during elections"'::jsonb, '"Article 14 and 21 cannot ever be considered together"'::jsonb, '"Article 21 protection includes scrutiny of the legal procedure affecting life and liberty; the existence of a procedure alone does not end analysis"'::jsonb, '"Speaker of the Assembly"'::jsonb, '"Governor"'::jsonb, '"District Collector"'::jsonb, '"Chief Minister"'::jsonb, '"Article 324"'::jsonb, '"Article 21"'::jsonb, '"Article 37"'::jsonb, '"Article 51A(k)"'::jsonb, '"Consider Part IV''s policy objective while separately testing implementation under Article 14 and relevant rights"'::jsonb, '"A welfare purpose removes the need for legal authority"'::jsonb, '"Directive Principles automatically excuse unequal treatment"'::jsonb, '"Only Article 324 applies to all government actions"'::jsonb, '"A private affidavit"'::jsonb, '"Preamble"'::jsonb, '"Schedule of office hours"'::jsonb, '"A municipal budget"'::jsonb, '"The basic structure doctrine"'::jsonb, '"Article 51A only"'::jsonb, '"The ordinary rule for email notices"'::jsonb, '"The municipal corporation framework"'::jsonb, '"Freedom of speech under Article 19 only"'::jsonb, '"Equality before law and equal protection under Article 14"'::jsonb, '"Election administration under Article 324"'::jsonb, '"Fundamental Duty under Article 51A only"'::jsonb, '"Only the Preamble sets out local election procedures"'::jsonb, '"The Preamble is the same as Article 51A"'::jsonb, '"The Preamble overrides all operative Articles"'::jsonb, '"The Preamble expresses constitutional values and aids interpretation; it does not independently grant unlimited executive authority"'::jsonb, '"Article 14 only concerns local elections"'::jsonb, '"Article 14 abolishes all classification"'::jsonb, '"Equality requires equal protection and bars arbitrary discrimination, but