udent says Fundamental Duties and Fundamental Rights are identical because both appear in the Constitution. Which correction is strongest?"'::jsonb, '"An amendment is challenged as destroying a foundational feature such as constitutional supremacy. Which case-law doctrine is relevant to the course''s basic-structure topic?"'::jsonb, '"Which statement best describes the ECI''s constitutional role?"'::jsonb, '"A public authority refuses the same legal protection to two people in materially identical circumstances without a relevant reason. Which constitutional principle is most directly raised?"'::jsonb, '"A Governor receives advice from a state''s Council of Ministers for ordinary state executive business. Which official is the normal political head of that Council?"'::jsonb, '"The Constitution''s Preamble is invoked to interpret an ambiguous provision. Which description best fits its role?"'::jsonb, '"A person argues that the Constitution exists only to empower the government. Which Preamble value most clearly contradicts an unlimited-power view?"'::jsonb, '"A district administration office is implementing state policy and coordinating local public services. Which level is most directly represented?"'::jsonb, '"A district officer administers relief in the district and coordinates local departments. Which syllabus topic is most directly illustrated?"'::jsonb, '"A state makes policy to improve public health and welfare. Which constitutional part is especially relevant as guiding principles for State policy?"'::jsonb, '"A school textbook says Fundamental Duties were added to the Constitution through an amendment. Which pairing is correct?"'::jsonb, '"A municipality''s constitutional framework is being discussed. Which Part was added for urban local bodies by the 74th Amendment?"'::jsonb, '"A State Election Commission plans local-body elections, but a student says Article 324 alone assigns the ECI all elections of every kind. Which correction is best?"'::jsonb, '"A public authority treats people unequally and also restricts a citizen''s speech. Which two provisions are the most direct starting points for analysis?"'::jsonb, '"A local body has been asked to handle city-level services rather than district rural planning. Which institution is a better fit?"'::jsonb, '"A citizen''s speech is restricted by a law. Which is the most accurate way to evaluate the restriction under Article 19?"'::jsonb, '"A government policy promotes public health but a person argues it is a Directive Principle. Which statement best distinguishes its legal status from a Fundamental Right?"'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"The Chief Election Commissioner runs municipal elections in each city directly"'::jsonb, '"The ECI handles Parliament and State Legislature elections; State ECs handle Panchayat and municipal elections"'::jsonb, '"The State EC appoints the President"'::jsonb, '"Both are the same officer under all circumstances"'::jsonb, '"All policies in Part IV are criminal provisions"'::jsonb, '"Part IV is the same as Part III"'::jsonb, '"Article 37 states Directive Principles are not enforceable by courts, while remaining fundamental in governance"'::jsonb, '"Part IV applies only during elections"'::jsonb, '"Article 21 protection of life and personal liberty"'::jsonb, '"Article 51A only"'::jsonb, '"Article 324 only"'::jsonb, '"Article 14 only in every possible case"'::jsonb, '"Duty to serve as a judge"'::jsonb, '"Duty to vote in every election as stated in Article 51A"'::jsonb, '"Duty to protect the environment only"'::jsonb, '"Duty to safeguard public property and abjure violence"'::jsonb, '"Collective responsibility of the Union Council of Ministers to Lok Sabha"'::jsonb, '"The independence of the State Election Commission"'::jsonb, '"Fundamental Duties under Article 51A"'::jsonb, '"Governor''s appointment power"'::jsonb, '"Treat Directive Principles as automatically unenforceable in every policy decision"'::jsonb, '"Read the provisions harmoniously, recognizing Part IV''s guidance and Part III''s enforceable rights"'::jsonb, '"Use Part IV as the sole source of criminal offences"'::jsonb, '"Ignore all Fundamental Rights"'::jsonb, '"All Fundamental Rights can be cancelled by an ordinary officer"'::jsonb, '"Article 21 applies only to elected legislators"'::jsonb, '"Part III contains only non-binding policy aims"'::jsonb, '"Some rights, including Article 19 freedoms, are subject to constitutionally specified restrictions"'::jsonb, '"Doctrine of double taxation only"'::jsonb, '"Doctrine of colourable printing"'::jsonb, '"Basic structure doctrine"'::jsonb, '"Principle of absolute parliamentary supremacy"'::jsonb, '"Parliament is the Union legislature; the Council of Ministers is part of the executive"'::jsonb, '"The Governor presides over both Houses of Parliament"'::jsonb, '"The Supreme Court is one of Parliament''s Houses"'::jsonb, '"The Election Commission debates and enacts all laws"'::jsonb, '"Article 19 requires free university education in every case"'::jsonb, '"Article 21A is a Fundamental Duty"'::jsonb, '"Article 51A(k) addresses providing educational opportunities to a child/ward aged 6–14"'::jsonb, '"Article 14 requires every parent to be a teacher"'::jsonb, '"Governor personally conducts both"'::jsonb, '"Municipal Corporation runs both elections"'::jsonb, '"Election Commission of India for Lok Sabha; State Election Commission for municipal elections"'::jsonb, '"State Election Commission conducts both in every case"'::jsonb, '"73rd Amendment"'::jsonb, '"52nd Amendment"'::jsonb, '"74th Amendment"'::jsonb, '"42nd Amendment"'::jsonb, '"Articles 75 and 164"'::jsonb, '"Articles 14 and 21"'::jsonb, '"Articles 51A and 324 only"'::jsonb, '"Articles 243K and 243ZA"'::jsonb, '"Both sets apply only to the President"'::jsonb, '"Duties are found only in local bylaws"'::jsonb, '"Rights are found only in Part IV"'::jsonb, '"Fundamental Rights are enforceable rights in Part III; Fundamental Duties are listed for citizens in Part IVA"'::jsonb, '"Doctrine of parliamentary privilege only"'::jsonb, '"Local election rotation"'::jsonb, '"Directive Principles'' non-justiciability"'::jsonb, '"Basic structure doctrine"'::jsonb, '"It administers all municipal services"'::jsonb, '"It appoints all Governors"'::jsonb, '"It makes all criminal laws"'::jsonb, '"It supervises specified electoral rolls and elections under Article 324"'::jsonb, '"Equality before law and equal protection under Article 14"'::jsonb, '"Fundamental Duty under Article 51A only"'::jsonb, '"Election administration under Article 324"'::jsonb, '"Freedom of speech under Article 19 only"'::jsonb, '"Chief Minister"'::jsonb, '"President"'::jsonb, '"Chief Election Commissioner"'::jsonb, '"Lok Sabha Speaker"'::jsonb, '"A source of unrestricted executive power"'::jsonb, '"A useful aid expressing constitutional objectives and values, read with the text rather than replacing it"'::jsonb, '"A separate criminal code replacing all Articles"'::jsonb, '"A local-government regulation"'::jsonb, '"Abolition of judicial review"'::jsonb, '"Unlimited terms for every elected body"'::jsonb, '"Justice, liberty, equality and fraternity as constitutional objectives"'::jsonb, '"Absolute executive discretion"'::jsonb, '"Union Legislature"'::jsonb, '"District administration"'::jsonb, '"Municipal Corporation only in every case"'::jsonb, '"Supreme Court Registry"'::jsonb, '"State election of Rajya Sabha members"'::jsonb, '"District administration"'::jsonb, '"Preamble interpretation only"'::jsonb, '"Union Parliament procedure"'::jsonb, '"Part XV only"'::jsonb, '"Part II"'::jsonb, '"Part IV"'::jsonb, '"Part IVA only"'::jsonb, '"74th Amendment, Article 21"'::jsonb, '"42nd Amendment, Part IVA/Article 51A"'::jsonb, '"44th Amendment, Part II"'::jsonb, '"73rd Amendment, Article 19"'::jsonb, '"Part II"'::jsonb, '"Part IXA"'::jsonb, '"Part III"'::jsonb, '"Part IVA"'::jsonb, '"All elections are conducted by municipal commissioners"'::jsonb, '"Article 324 deals only with sc